@[expose] public section

/-!
# Associated primes in the closed fibre of a flat module over a valuation ring

Let `A` be a valuation ring, `A → B` a local homomorphism of local rings which is essentially
of finite type, and `N` a finite `B`-module which is flat over `A`. This file proves that a
prime `q` of `B` which is associated to `N` *after localizing at `q`*, and whose sum with
`𝔪_A B` has radical `𝔪_B`, forces `𝔪_B` to be an associated prime of the closed fibre
`N/𝔪_A N`.

That is the local, purely ring-theoretic content of the valuation-ring case of Stacks 0GSI —
the final paragraph of that lemma's proof, to which the general statement is reduced. In the
geometry, `q` is the prime of `𝒪_{X,x}` belonging to a relative associated point `y` of a
finite-type quasi-coherent module in the generic fibre of `X → Spec A`, the radical condition
says the closed point of `Spec 𝒪_{X,x}` is a generic point of the closed fibre of the closure
of `y`, and the conclusion says that point is a relative associated point too.

## Main results

* `exists_smul_eq_of_mem_smul_top`: over a valuation ring, every element of
  `I • (⊤ : Submodule A N)` is a *single* multiple `a • n` with `a ∈ I`.
* `restrictScalars_map_smul_top`: reducing `N` modulo the ideal `𝔪_A B` generated by `𝔪_A` in
  `B` agrees with reducing it modulo `𝔪_A` over `A`.
* `injective_smul_of_mem_smul_top`: the case `u = (g • ·)` of Stacks 0GSG — multiplication by
  `g : B` is injective on `N` as soon as it is injective on the closed fibre.
* `maximalIdeal_mem_associatedPrimes_quotient`: the statement above.
* `maximalIdeal_mem_associatedPrimes_quotient_of_mem_associatedPrimes`: the same with the
  hypothesis on `q` read over `B` rather than over the localization at `q`, which is the
  weaker of the two.

## Implementation notes

Nothing is narrowed: all four results are universe-polymorphic in `A`, `B` and `N`
independently, and `B` is *not* assumed Noetherian — it is not, in the geometric application,
since a valuation ring need not be.

`injective_smul_of_mem_smul_top` is proved without the limit argument of Stacks 046Y that the
general 0GSG needs. Flatness over the valuation ring `A` makes `N` torsion-free, and
`exists_smul_eq_of_mem_smul_top` then gives `Ker (g • ·) = 𝔪_A · Ker (g • ·)` directly: an
element `n` of the kernel lies in `𝔪_A N` by hypothesis, so is `a • n'` with `a ∈ 𝔪_A`, and
`a • (g • n') = g • n = 0` with `a ≠ 0` forces `n'` into the kernel as well. Locality of
`A → B` upgrades this to `Ker ≤ 𝔪_B · Ker`, and Nakayama finishes, the kernel being finitely
generated by Stacks 0GSE — which is where the two finiteness hypotheses are spent. The general
0GSG, for an arbitrary map of finite modules, is not needed and is not reproved here.

The hypothesis on `q` is the *localized* one, `𝔪_{B_q} ∈ Ass_{B_q}(N_q)`, and not the global
`q ∈ Ass_B(N)`. This is not a stylistic choice. Stacks' proof of 0GSI has only the localized
form available — in the geometry it is the statement that a point of the generic fibre is a
relative associated point, which is a condition on the *stalk* at that point — and descending
from it to the global form is Stacks 0310 (2), in `Module.associatedPrimes` as
`comap_mem_associatedPrimes_of_mem_associatedPrimes_of_isLocalizedModule_of_fg`,
whose `q.FG` hypothesis is unavailable: `B` is only essentially of finite type over a
valuation ring, so it need not be Noetherian. The localized form is also the weaker
hypothesis, hence this the stronger theorem; the global version is recovered from it in
`maximalIdeal_mem_associatedPrimes_quotient_of_mem_associatedPrimes` by Stacks 0310 (1), which
needs no finiteness. Only the proof's final step is affected: the element `g ∈ q` produced by
prime avoidance is regular on `N`, and regularity survives localization
(`IsSMulRegular.of_isLocalizedModule`), which is all the localized hypothesis needs.

`maximalIdeal_mem_associatedPrimes_quotient` is stated with associated primes over `B`, not
over `B ⧸ 𝔪_A B`, so that no quotient-ring module structure appears in the statement. The
proof builds that structure internally — the fibre is `𝔪_A B`-torsion, so
`Module.IsTorsionBySet.module` applies — because the finiteness of the set of associated
primes is only available over `B ⧸ 𝔪_A B`, which *is* Noetherian: it is essentially of finite
type over the residue field of `A`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GSI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GSI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GSG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GSG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GSE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GSE)
-/

open IsLocalRing Submodule

namespace Stacks.ValuationRingFibre

/-- Over a valuation ring every element of `I • (⊤ : Submodule A N)` is already a single
multiple `a • n` with `a ∈ I`: the finitely many coefficients occurring in a sum are totally
ordered by divisibility, so one of them divides the rest. -/
theorem exists_smul_eq_of_mem_smul_top {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [ValuationRing A]
    {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] {I : Ideal A} {x : N}
    (hx : x ∈ I • (⊤ : Submodule A N)) : ∃ a ∈ I, ∃ n : N, x = a • n := by
  refine Submodule.smul_induction_on hx (fun a ha n _ ↦ ⟨a, ha, n, rfl⟩) ?_
  rintro x y ⟨a, ha, n, rfl⟩ ⟨b, hb, m, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hc | hc⟩ := ValuationRing.cond a b
  · exact ⟨a, ha, n + c • m, by rw [smul_add, ← hc, mul_smul]⟩
  · exact ⟨b, hb, c • n + m, by rw [smul_add, ← hc, mul_smul]⟩

section Bridge

variable {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
  {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module B N] [IsScalarTower A B N]

/-- The `A`-submodule `I • (⊤ : Submodule A N)` is stable under the `B`-action. -/
theorem smul_mem_smul_top {I : Ideal A} (b : B) {x : N}
    (hx : x ∈ I • (⊤ : Submodule A N)) : b • x ∈ I • (⊤ : Submodule A N) := by
  refine Submodule.smul_induction_on hx (fun a ha n _ ↦ ?_) (fun x y hx hy ↦ ?_)
  · rw [smul_comm]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul ha Submodule.mem_top
  · rw [smul_add]
    exact Submodule.add_mem _ hx hy

/-- Reducing `N` modulo the ideal generated by `I` in `B` is the same as reducing it modulo `I`
over `A`. -/
theorem restrictScalars_map_smul_top (I : Ideal A) :
    ((I.map (algebraMap A B)) • (⊤ : Submodule B N)).restrictScalars A
      = I • (⊤ : Submodule A N) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun x hx ↦ ?_) (Submodule.smul_le.2 fun a ha n _ ↦ ?_)
  · let T : Ideal B :=
      { carrier := {r : B | ∀ n : N, r • n ∈ I • (⊤ : Submodule A N)}
        add_mem' := fun hr hs n ↦ by
          simpa [add_smul] using Submodule.add_mem _ (hr n) (hs n)
        zero_mem' := fun n ↦ by simp
        smul_mem' := fun b r hr n ↦ by
          rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_smul]
          exact smul_mem_smul_top b (hr n) }
    have hT : I.map (algebraMap A B) ≤ T :=
      Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun a ha n ↦ by
        rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul]
        exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul ha Submodule.mem_top
    exact Submodule.smul_induction_on (Submodule.restrictScalars_mem A _ x |>.mp hx)
      (fun r hr n _ ↦ hT hr n) fun x y hx hy ↦ Submodule.add_mem _ hx hy
  · rw [Submodule.restrictScalars_mem, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul B a n]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha) Submodule.mem_top

/-- Locality of `A → B` turns `𝔪_A`-multiples into `𝔪_B`-multiples. -/
theorem smul_le_restrictScalars_maximalIdeal_smul [IsLocalRing A] [IsLocalRing B]
    [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)] (K : Submodule B N) :
    maximalIdeal A • (K.restrictScalars A)
      ≤ Submodule.restrictScalars A (maximalIdeal B • K) := by
  refine Submodule.smul_le.2 fun a ha x hx ↦ ?_
  rw [Submodule.restrictScalars_mem, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul B a x]
  refine Submodule.smul_mem_smul ?_ ((Submodule.restrictScalars_mem A K x).mp hx)
  rw [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff]
  exact fun h ↦ (IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal a).mp ha (isUnit_of_map_unit _ a h)

end Bridge

/-- **The case `u = (g • ·)` of Stacks 0GSG.** Let `A` be a valuation ring, `A → B` a local
homomorphism of local rings which is essentially of finite type, and `N` a finite `B`-module
which is flat over `A`. If multiplication by `g : B` is injective on the closed fibre
`N/𝔪_A N`, then it is injective on `N`.

Unlike the general 0GSG this needs no limit argument: flatness of `N` over the valuation ring
`A` makes it torsion-free, and `exists_smul_eq_of_mem_smul_top` then shows directly that
`Ker (g • ·) = 𝔪_A · Ker (g • ·)`, whence Nakayama applies once the kernel is known to be
finitely generated — which is Stacks 0GSE. -/
theorem injective_smul_of_mem_smul_top
    {A B N : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [ValuationRing A]
    [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing B] [Algebra A B] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)]
    [Algebra.EssFiniteType A B]
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module B N] [IsScalarTower A B N]
    [Module.Finite B N] [Module.Flat A N] {g : B}
    (hg : ∀ n : N, g • n ∈ (maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A B) • (⊤ : Submodule B N) →
      n ∈ (maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A B) • (⊤ : Submodule B N)) :
    Function.Injective (LinearMap.lsmul B N g) := by
  have htf : Module.IsTorsionFree A N := Module.Flat.isTorsionFree
  set u : N →ₗ[B] N := LinearMap.lsmul B N g with hu
  have : Module.Flat A (LinearMap.range u) := by
    refine Module.Flat.flat_iff_torsion_eq_bot_of_isBezout.mpr ?_
    exact Submodule.isTorsionFree_iff_torsion_eq_bot.mp inferInstance
  have : Module.FinitePresentation B (LinearMap.range u) :=
    (essentiallyOfFinitePresentation_and_finitePresentation_of_flat_of_valuationRing
      (A := A) (B := B) (M := LinearMap.range u)).2 inferInstance inferInstance
  have hfg : (LinearMap.ker u).FG := by
    rw [← LinearMap.ker_rangeRestrict u]
    exact Module.FinitePresentation.fg_ker u.rangeRestrict u.surjective_rangeRestrict
  have hstep : (LinearMap.ker u).restrictScalars A
      ≤ maximalIdeal A • ((LinearMap.ker u).restrictScalars A) := by
    intro x hx
    have hgx : g • x = 0 := by
      simpa [hu] using (Submodule.restrictScalars_mem A _ x).mp hx
    have hmem : x ∈ maximalIdeal A • (⊤ : Submodule A N) := by
      rw [← restrictScalars_map_smul_top (A := A) (B := B) (N := N) (maximalIdeal A)]
      exact hg x (by rw [hgx]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _)
    obtain ⟨a, ha, n, rfl⟩ := exists_smul_eq_of_mem_smul_top hmem
    rcases eq_or_ne a 0 with rfl | ha0
    · simp
    · refine Submodule.smul_mem_smul ha ?_
      have : a • (g • n) = a • (0 : N) := by rw [smul_zero, ← smul_comm]; exact hgx
      simpa [hu, LinearMap.mem_ker] using LinearMap.lsmul_injective (M := N) ha0 this
  have hK : LinearMap.ker u ≤ maximalIdeal B • LinearMap.ker u := fun x hx ↦
    (Submodule.restrictScalars_mem A _ x).mp
      (smul_le_restrictScalars_maximalIdeal_smul (LinearMap.ker u)
        (hstep ((Submodule.restrictScalars_mem A _ x).mpr hx)))
  rw [← LinearMap.ker_eq_bot]
  exact Submodule.eq_bot_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson_bot (maximalIdeal B) (LinearMap.ker u) hfg hK
    (le_of_eq (IsLocalRing.jacobson_eq_maximalIdeal (⊥ : Ideal B) bot_ne_top).symm)

section Main

/-- The ideal of `B` generated by the maximal ideal of `A`. An `abbrev`, hence reducible, so
that the instances Mathlib provides for `B ⧸ (maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A B)` are found
for `B ⧸ baseIdeal A B` as well. -/
private abbrev baseIdeal (A : Type*) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [ValuationRing A]
    (B : Type*) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] : Ideal B :=
  (maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A B)

variable {A B N : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [ValuationRing A]
  [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing B] [Algebra A B] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)]
  [Algebra.EssFiniteType A B]
  [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module B N] [IsScalarTower A B N]
  [Module.Finite B N] [Module.Flat A N]

/-- **The valuation-ring core of Stacks 0GSI.** Let `A` be a valuation ring, `A → B` a local
homomorphism of local rings which is essentially of finite type, and `N` a finite `B`-module
flat over `A`. Let `q` be a prime of `B` whose maximal ideal is, after localizing at `q`, an
associated prime of `N_q`, and which together with the ideal generated by `𝔪_A` cuts out only
the closed point: `√(q + 𝔪_A B) = 𝔪_B`. Then `𝔪_B` is an associated prime of the closed fibre
`N/𝔪_A N`.

The localization is presented as data — any `B`-algebra `B_q` localizing `B` at `q` and any
`B`-linear `l : N → N_q` localizing `N` at `q` — so that a consumer whose localization arises
geometrically, as a stalk, can use it without transporting to `Localization.AtPrime q`.

Geometrically `q` is a relative associated point of a module in the generic fibre over a
valuation ring, the radical hypothesis says the closed point is a generic point of the closed
fibre of the closure of that point, and the conclusion is that the closed point is a relative
associated point too. -/
theorem maximalIdeal_mem_associatedPrimes_quotient {q : Ideal B} [q.IsPrime]
    {Bq Nq : Type*} [CommRing Bq] [Algebra B Bq] [IsLocalization.AtPrime Bq q] [IsLocalRing Bq]
    [AddCommGroup Nq] [Module B Nq] [Module Bq Nq] [IsScalarTower B Bq Nq]
    (l : N →ₗ[B] Nq) [IsLocalizedModule q.primeCompl l]
    (hqrad : (q ⊔ (maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A B)).radical = maximalIdeal B)
    (hq : maximalIdeal Bq ∈ associatedPrimes Bq Nq) :
    maximalIdeal B ∈ associatedPrimes B
      (N ⧸ ((maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A B) • (⊤ : Submodule B N))) := by
  classical
  change maximalIdeal B ∈ associatedPrimes B (N ⧸ (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N)))
  by_contra hcon
  -- The closed fibre is a module over `B ⧸ 𝔪_A B`, and that ring is Noetherian because it is
  -- essentially of finite type over the residue field of `A`.
  have htor : Module.IsTorsionBySet B (N ⧸ (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N)))
      (baseIdeal A B : Set B) := by
    intro x a
    obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mkQ_surjective (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N)) x
    rw [← map_smul, Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul a.2 Submodule.mem_top
  let : Module (B ⧸ baseIdeal A B) (N ⧸ (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N))) := htor.module
  have hmk : ∀ (b : B) (x : N ⧸ (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N))),
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (baseIdeal A B) b • x = b • x := fun _ _ ↦ rfl
  have : IsScalarTower B (B ⧸ baseIdeal A B)
      (N ⧸ (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N))) := htor.isScalarTower
  have : Module.Finite (B ⧸ baseIdeal A B) (N ⧸ (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N))) :=
    Module.Finite.of_restrictScalars_finite B _ _
  let : Field (A ⧸ maximalIdeal A) := Ideal.Quotient.field _
  have : IsNoetherianRing (B ⧸ baseIdeal A B) :=
    Algebra.EssFiniteType.isNoetherianRing (A ⧸ maximalIdeal A) _
  -- An associated prime of the fibre over `B ⧸ 𝔪_A B` pulls back to one over `B`.
  have hpull : ∀ p : Ideal (B ⧸ baseIdeal A B),
      p ∈ associatedPrimes (B ⧸ baseIdeal A B) (N ⧸ (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N))) →
      p.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (baseIdeal A B)) ∈
        associatedPrimes B (N ⧸ (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N))) := by
    rintro p ⟨hprime, x, rfl⟩
    have := hprime
    refine ⟨Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _, x, ?_⟩
    rw [Ideal.comap_radical]
    rfl
  -- Hence no associated prime of the fibre contains the image of `q`: one that did would
  -- contain `√(q + 𝔪_A B) = 𝔪_B`, so would be `𝔪_B`, which `hcon` forbids.
  have hnotle : ∀ p ∈ associatedPrimes (B ⧸ baseIdeal A B)
      (N ⧸ (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N))),
      ¬ q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (baseIdeal A B)) ≤ p := by
    intro p hp hle
    have : p.IsPrime := (AssociatedPrimes.mem_iff.mp hp).isPrime
    have h1 : q ⊔ baseIdeal A B ≤ p.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (baseIdeal A B)) := by
      refine sup_le (fun b hb ↦ hle (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hb)) fun b hb ↦ ?_
      simp [Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr hb]
    have h2 : maximalIdeal B ≤ p.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (baseIdeal A B)) := by
      rw [← hqrad]
      exact (Ideal.radical_mono h1).trans
        (le_of_eq (Ideal.IsPrime.radical (Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _)))
    exact hcon <| ((maximalIdeal.isMaximal B).eq_of_le
      (Ideal.comap_isPrime (Ideal.Quotient.mk (baseIdeal A B)) p).ne_top h2) ▸ hpull p hp
  -- Prime avoidance: the associated primes of the fibre are finitely many, so `q` has an
  -- element acting as a nonzerodivisor on the fibre.
  have hfin := associatedPrimes.finite (B ⧸ baseIdeal A B)
    (N ⧸ (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N)))
  have hnotsub : ¬ ((q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (baseIdeal A B)) : Set (B ⧸ baseIdeal A B)) ⊆
      ⋃ p ∈ associatedPrimes (B ⧸ baseIdeal A B)
        (N ⧸ (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N))), (p : Set (B ⧸ baseIdeal A B))) := by
    intro h
    obtain ⟨p, hp, hle⟩ := (Ideal.subset_union_prime_finite hfin (f := id) 0 0
      fun i hi _ _ ↦ (AssociatedPrimes.mem_iff.mp hi).isPrime).1 h
    exact hnotle p hp hle
  obtain ⟨gbar, hgbar, hgbarnot⟩ := Set.not_subset.mp hnotsub
  rw [biUnion_associatedPrimes_eq_zero_divisors (B ⧸ baseIdeal A B)
    (N ⧸ (baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N)))] at hgbarnot
  obtain ⟨g, hgq, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_map_iff_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective |>.mp hgbar
  -- That element is injective on the fibre, hence, by 0GSG, on `N` itself.
  have hg : ∀ n : N, g • n ∈ baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N) →
      n ∈ baseIdeal A B • (⊤ : Submodule B N) := by
    intro n hn
    by_contra hnot
    refine hgbarnot ⟨Submodule.mkQ _ n, ?_, ?_⟩
    · simp [Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero, hnot]
    · rw [hmk, ← map_smul, Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
      exact hn
  have hreg : IsSMulRegular N g := injective_smul_of_mem_smul_top (A := A) hg
  -- Injectivity of multiplication by `g` survives localization at `q`. There `𝔪_{B_q}` is the
  -- radical of the annihilator of some `ξ : N_q`, and `g ∈ q` then forces `ξ = 0`.
  have hregq : IsSMulRegular Nq (algebraMap B Bq g) :=
    hreg.of_isLocalizedModule Bq q.primeCompl l
  obtain ⟨hmprime, ξ, hξ⟩ := hq
  have hgm : algebraMap B Bq g ∈ maximalIdeal Bq :=
    (IsLocalization.AtPrime.to_map_mem_maximal_iff Bq q g).mpr hgq
  rw [hξ] at hgm
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := Ideal.mem_radical_iff.mp hgm
  have hzero : ξ = 0 := by
    refine hregq.pow k ?_
    simpa using Submodule.mem_colon_singleton.mp hk
  refine hmprime.ne_top ?_
  rw [hξ, hzero]
  exact (Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _).mpr (Ideal.mem_radical_iff.mpr ⟨1, by simp⟩)

/-- **The valuation-ring core of Stacks 0GSI, with the global hypothesis.** The form of
`maximalIdeal_mem_associatedPrimes_quotient` in which `q` is assumed to be an associated prime
of `N` over `B` itself.

This is strictly the weaker statement: an associated prime stays associated after localizing at
itself (`Module.associatedPrimes.mem_associatedPrimes_atPrime_of_mem_associatedPrimes`, Stacks
0310 (1)), with no finite-generation hypothesis, whereas the converse descent needs `q.FG` —
which is unavailable here, `B` being only essentially of finite type over a valuation ring and
hence not Noetherian. -/
theorem maximalIdeal_mem_associatedPrimes_quotient_of_mem_associatedPrimes {q : Ideal B}
    (hqrad : (q ⊔ (maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A B)).radical = maximalIdeal B)
    (hq : q ∈ associatedPrimes B N) :
    maximalIdeal B ∈ associatedPrimes B
      (N ⧸ ((maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A B) • (⊤ : Submodule B N))) :=
  have : q.IsPrime := hq.isPrime
  maximalIdeal_mem_associatedPrimes_quotient (A := A) (Bq := Localization.AtPrime q)
    (LocalizedModule.mkLinearMap q.primeCompl N) hqrad
    (Module.associatedPrimes.mem_associatedPrimes_atPrime_of_mem_associatedPrimes hq)

end Main

end Stacks.ValuationRingFibre
